---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Do you run sober living houses?', a: "No — we refer to them rather than operate them, and we are clear about that so nobody arrives expecting something different. What we do have is a working knowledge of the good ones in the Phoenix area and across Arizona, and your case manager will make an introduction rather than hand you a printout." },
  { q: 'I have nowhere to go right now. Can I still come?', a: "Yes, and please say so on the first call. Detox and residential are live-in, so treatment itself answers the housing question for the first month or so — and that stretch is when the longer-term answer gets worked out with someone helping you." },
  { q: 'Where I live now makes it impossible to stay sober.', a: "That is one of the most useful things you can tell us, and it will not be held against you. Going home to the same room is how a lot of good stays come undone, so knowing it up front changes what your discharge plan is built around." },
  { q: 'What does sober living cost?', a: "It varies by house, and since these are independent operations the house quotes its own rate rather than us quoting it for them. Ask us on the call and we will point you at options in a range that works, including ones that some programmes help cover." },
  { q: 'Can I go into sober living straight away instead of treatment?', a: "Sober living generally expects you to be stable already — it is somewhere to live, not clinical care. If you are still drinking or using daily, detox first is both safer and usually what a house will want to see. We can help you sequence it." },
  { q: 'Will my insurance pay for sober living?', a: "Housing usually sits outside what a health plan covers, though some programmes attach housing support to their own services. It is worth asking about specifically, and we will tell you what we know rather than leaving you to find out at the door." },
  { q: 'When does the housing conversation start?', a: "Early in your stay, not the week you leave. Discharge planning runs alongside the clinical work precisely so that the last few days are not spent scrambling." },
  { q: 'What if I want to go back to my family instead?', a: "Then that is the plan, and family work is part of the programme so it can be prepared for properly on both sides. There is no expectation that everyone ends up in sober living." },
];
---
<section id="sober-living-faq" class="bg-cream py-[70px]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
      Straight answers
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-10">Questions about housing</h2>
    <div class="divide-y divide-cream-soft border-t border-b border-cream-soft">
      {faqs.map(f => (
        <details class="group py-5">
          <summary class="flex items-start justify-between gap-6 cursor-pointer">
            <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-charcoal text-[18px] leading-[28px]">{f.q}</h3>
            <span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-teal">
              <svg class="faq-plus w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
              <svg class="faq-minus w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" d="M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[27px] mt-4 pr-10">{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
